<p></p>



<p>We see butterflies and fruits in the foreground in Damien Hirst's work titled Love and Outside of Love, which is given above. The theme of death, which also takes place in contemporary art, now comes to the fore in performance arts and live shows. While butterflies in Hirst's work show the transience of life, fruit likewise depicts the body's decay and transience after death. As it is seen, the death theme did not affect only one period. In different periods, death was handled in different depictions by different artists.</p>



